ambassador:
And had my friend,—for Nature comes sometimes
And says, ‘I am ambassador for God.’
I felt the wind soft from the land of souls;

amble:
You need n't bothah 'roun' yo'se'f,
Somebody's boun' to amble in
An' 'vite you to dey co'n meal bin;

amber:
The winter will be short, the summer long,
The autumn amber-hued, sunny and hot,
Tasting of cider and of scuppernong;

ambient:
In the grove's dark recesses pours his moan;
Each branch, wide-spreading to the ambient sky,
Forgets its verdure, and submits to die.

ambers:
Were quaint devices;
Patterns in ambers,
And in the clouded green of jades.
